# CRITICAL: NO DOCUMENTATION FILES IN DOTFILES

## ABSOLUTE PROHIBITION ON DOCUMENTATION FILES

You MUST NEVER create documentation files (.md, .txt, README, guides, etc.) in dotfiles unless the user EXPLICITLY asks for a specific documentation file.

### What is FORBIDDEN:

- ❌ Creating README.md files
- ❌ Creating any .md files (guides, documentation, comparisons, etc.)
- ❌ Creating setup guides, migration guides, comparison documents
- ❌ Creating "helpful" documentation
- ❌ ANY documentation file creation without EXPLICIT request

### What is ALLOWED:

- ✅ Creating scripts (.sh files)
- ✅ Creating config files (.conf, .json, .yaml, etc.)
- ✅ Inline comments in code
- ✅ Verbal explanations in chat

### This Applies To:

- All subdirectories in dotfiles
- All projects
- All AI agents (Cursor AI, Composer, etc.)
- All future sessions

### Rule:

**SCRIPTS AND CONFIGS ONLY. NO DOCUMENTATION. EXPLAIN VERBALLY.**
